{
  "abstract_summary": "An agent that stores facts over time eventually stores several versions of the same fact. Asked a value-agnostic question - \"which team does X play for now?\" - a similarity retriever cannot prefer the current version, because every version matches the entity the query names. StaleBench isolates this stale-retrieval...",
